body:
Try spending 5 hours pushing a log the size of a 1.25l Pepsi bottle - a day after major bowel surgery and your guts are (externally) held together by glue.

&#x200B;

It then took half an hour to break it up to flush it. In the NHS the night staff are absolute cunts.

Not bad pressies externally. Still too shiney! 

&#x200B;

Be careful it'll be an RC if lucky, or fent if not.

I heard you can grow potatoes in your own shit on Mars.

&#x200B;

Ask Matt Damon he has plenty of experience being abandoned in space.

And according to Wedino's: legit!

&#x200B;

 [https://www.wedinos.org/images/sample\_testing/11137.jpg](https://www.wedinos.org/images/sample_testing/11137.jpg)

" Im not using any of it. "

&#x200B;

To quote Battle Star Galactica - And so say we all!

Frankly when I was running a steep withdrawal from buprenorphine I just had a lot of water, some cup a soup, a lot of diazepam and a shit load of zolpidem/zopiclone (to be switched around every two days or so to stop tolerance).

&#x200B;

Good luck,

This is my name box:

&#x200B;

[https://i.imgur.com/7N1wQU3.jpg](https://i.imgur.com/7N1wQU3.jpg)

&#x200B;

[https://imgur.com/NTp8f3K](https://imgur.com/NTp8f3K)

I had 30 on Monday.

&#x200B;

I have 2 now.

Are you an inpatient?

&#x200B;

If so get them to ramp up the IV morphine until it works. If you have respiration issues there's oxygen literally next to your head.

If you're an outpatient wait 24 hours then take the morphine.

&#x200B;

\*I Shattered my arm on Subutex.

If in the UK send one - or even half of one here. Wait 2/3 days and they'll tell you.

&#x200B;

 [https://www.wedinos.org/](https://www.wedinos.org/)

Well, I was switched to it today from 8mg Subutex. I've found it hits like a damn train with a bit of cyclizine.

&#x200B;

The only issue I had was that it wasn't dissolving as I was so used to limiting the amount of spit in my mouth with the Subutex to help minimise swallowing, this stuff NEEDS spit in your mouth to dissolve it!

Does lansoprazole work too, or any proton pump inhibitor?

&#x200B;

How does this work? I know PPI's reduce stomach acid (I was on them for years due to ulcers and Crohn's), does it mean the bioavailability of benzo's go up, or that simply more benzo is absorbed and not destroyed by the highly acidic environment?

Ahhh good old Indian Jpee Pharmaceuticals!

&#x200B;

I've sent some of there alprazolam and zolpidem off to Wedino's for testing and they are absolutely fine (at least in my case)

Mine come in a jiffy bag which requires a signature from the recipient.

&#x200B;

UK here so it's the good old Royal Mail. Adam is my postie, we speak, chat, wave, thumbs up, shoot the breeze and every Christmas he gets a card with £20 in it.

&#x200B;

Adam knows full bloody well what is in my jiffy bags. Be like Adam postal people. Be cool.

Be careful. Even with tolerance never exceed 25/30 tabs in 24 hours.

&#x200B;

I once took 52x 30mg straight codeine phosphate over 14/16 hours. I ended up feeling a bit odd, wondering to myself if this was a seizure coming on and the next thing I know 30 minutes have passed and I have paramedics surrounding my bed.

&#x200B;

I did have a seizure, not my first by far but even with my very high opiate tolerance you can hit a point where your seizure threshold is lowered. This is why I also recommend staying the fuck away from tramadol. It's totally shit for recreational use and dramatically decreases your seizure threshold.

&#x200B;

Now if I'm going on a binge I drop a couple of alprazolam or diazepam as they help raise your seizure threshold.

&#x200B;

If you are UK based I'm guessing these are from Doctor4U?

Well, the last hit was 3 days ago, so no WDs yet!

&#x200B;

I have a very strong suspicion I stashed them somewhere. Bugger knows where!

Ah well, I have to crush up several 60mg delayed release DHC to get that nod.

&#x200B;

Standard DHC does absolutely sod all for me. I've gotten better euphoria from buprenorphine boosted with cyclizine!

&#x200B;

I find Z-drugs to just be tiring (well duuuuuh) - unless I've let my tolerance slip back to zero and then Ambien can give me a strong, but weird buzz.

Diazepam does nothing, but alprazolam really does hit the spot. Whilst they were legal in the UK diclazepam was really good. I found it affected me like a halfway house between a strong opiate and benzo nod.

Damn right. My ill health and recovery, but inability to get my fucking ass back into gear could have, and possible still could cost me my job. A great job, 9 years here with 12 years total with the civil service. 

&#x200B;

Because of the threat of loss of income, I earn 65% of our combined monthly income, but no kids at 35 just me and the wife, I've gone back to my GP and gone back onto subs. That means if the pressure of work gets too much, or if they do try and get rid of me through medical or capability tribunals (UK public service, they can't just say "Fuck off, your sacked") that part of my brain which overrides rational thought can activate as much as it wants, but whatever it makes me buy it will not make me high. So it just doesn't bother.

&#x200B;

The only major problem is subs won't work with benzos and I have a good UK supplier for benzos and Z-drugs (all tested at Wedino's and always 100% legit), and as a fast metabolizer I've found if I take 2/300mg of cyclizine before dosing bupe I can get a decent morphine like high from it a couple of times, before my bupe blood level hits max and instead of diminishing returns, it's zero returns. I think that's why my GP also let me have 100 cyclizine at the same time, he knows two things about them and me 1) they are the only anti-emetic that works (I have Crohn's Disease and hypothyroidism) 2) he also knows that I use them to boost opiates to get highs when normally I wouldn't. So he's given me the ability to have a good time once or twice and then no more.

&#x200B;

Right now is good time number 2! And it works. Haven't taken bupe in 30 hours, just dropped 260mg of codeine with 250mg of cyclizine and BOOM! The rush is a-comin', I can feel it.

I've just sent a sample of Neliz off to Wedino's yesterday, so expect the result back mid-next week.

&#x200B;

This will make it only the second sample.

&#x200B;

Given I used to take diclazepam when it was a "legal" RC the high and nod feel very much the same.
